review:
TOP app, but don’t rely on in-game scaling if image quality matters to you. Leave the game at its default resolution (1920x1080, etc.), just set it to fullscreen borderless windowed mode.

GUIDE FOR THE APP:
first of all, go to the app settings and set Start as administrator to On, Start at Windows startup to Off (I launch the app right before the game) Minimize to tray to On, Close to tray to On;

already in the main menu of the app set: Scaling Type to LS1 (for 3D games), Sharpness to 0 or 1 or whatever you prefer, Performance to Off, Scaling Mode to Custom, Factor to 1, Resize before scaling to Off;

Frame Generation: Type set LSFG 3.1 (the latest version at the moment); Mode to Fixed , Multiplier to 2 (if higher, artifacts like a blurry screen will appear), Flow Scale to 75% or 100% depends from picture in game;

Capture: API set WGC, Queue target to 1;

Cursor: On Off Off Off;

Rendering: Sync mode to Vsync, Max frame latency to 10 (not for fps games bc it cause delay), HDR support depending on your monitor (if supported and if you need it), G-Sync support to On (with Nvidia gpu), Draw FPS to On if you want to see realFPS/createdFPS;

GPU and Display: Auto, Auto;

Crop Input: all set to zero;

Behavior: Multi-display mode to Off.
and that`s it :0
